Translation patch: `value::convert::time`: time calls go through `trusted`

Change: `time::Month::try_from`, `month as u8`, `Date::from_calendar_date`, `Time::from_hms_micro`, `PrimitiveDateTime::new`, the `Date`/`Time` getters, `Date::parse`/`Time::parse`/`PrimitiveDateTime::parse` with each format description (moved to trusted.rs), `Parse::TryFromParsed(TryFromParsed::InsufficientInformation)`, `from_utf8`, `str::len` (as `trusted::str_as_bytes(s).len()`), and the `time::Duration` constructors, `+`, `-`, unary `-`, `< Duration::ZERO` and `whole_*` become `trusted::time_*` helpers; `a + b + c` becomes `time_duration_add(time_duration_add(a, b), c)`. For a `PrimitiveDateTime x`, the date getters go through `x.date()` and the time getters through `x.time()`. `from_utf8(b).map_err(|_| e)` becomes `trusted::str_from_utf8(b).ok_or_else(|| e)`.
Why: time is not translated (see patch 40).
Behaviour: Identical: the same calls in the same order (operands left to right, then the operator); time 0.3.55's `PrimitiveDateTime` getters return those of its `date()`/`time()`; `str::len` is `as_bytes().len()`.

